/**
 * @defgroup MCC_Notation Notation
 * @ingroup MCC
 * @brief Text formatting and parsing into caller-provided buffers.
 *
 * `MCC::Notation::Format()` writes note names, pitches, intervals and, when
 * their modules are enabled, catalog scales, chord symbols and keys. Output
 * follows `snprintf` semantics in code units and never allocates
 * (SPEC-TXT-1..2). ASCII symbols are the default (`C#4`, `Bbb`, `AA4`);
 * `NotationOptions::symbols` selects Unicode accidentals (`C♯4`, `B𝄫`) and
 * `explicitNatural` writes the natural sign (SPEC-TXT-3). The buffer type
 * selects the encoding: `char` for ASCII or UTF-8, `char16_t` for UTF-16 and
 * `char32_t` for UTF-32 (SPEC-TXT-5). A `CodePointSink` overload sends each
 * code point to a callback instead, so text can go straight to a serial port
 * or display without a buffer. `ParseNoteName()`, `ParsePitch()` and
 * `ParseInterval()` read any of the three encodings, ASCII or Unicode
 * symbols, either letter case and `x` for the double sharp, and return the
 * invalid value on malformed text (SPEC-TXT-4). Text constants are stored in
 * program memory on AVR.
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * char text[16];
 * MCC::Notation::Format(text, sizeof(text), MCC::Notation::ParsePitch("F#3"));  // "F#3"
 * MCC::Notation::Format(text, sizeof(text), root, MCC::Chords::Id::HalfDiminishedSeventh);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Available when `MCC_NOTATION` is defined. Requires the Interval module.
 */
